data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/mission-report.md\", \"content\": \"# Mission report: greet, tested\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\n## What was delivered\\n\\ndev (branch `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, commit `cbec32114883411dcb1beb84800c00a21b88a486`\\non the `subject` repo) added:\\n\\n- `src/greet.py`:\\n  ```python\\n  def greet(name):\\n      return f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"\\n  ```\\n- `tests/test_greet.py`: unittest `TestCase` with `test_normal_name`\\n  (`greet(\\\"Ada\\\") == \\\"Hello, Ada!\\\"`) and `test_empty_string`\\n  (`greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`), with `src` added to `sys.path` so\\n  `unittest discover` can import `greet` without packaging.\\n\\n## Verification performed by the orchestrator (not just dev's self-report)\\n\\n- Fetched dev's branch (`cs-campaign-member fetch dev`) and confirmed via\\n  `git diff \u003cbase\u003e..campaign/dev/subject --stat` that the only changes were\\n  the two new files (21 lines added, nothing removed/altered elsewhere).\\n- Read both files directly at the commit to confirm `greet()`'s exact\\n  behavior and that the tests cover a normal name and the empty string as\\n  the mission requires.\\n- Extracted the committed tree with `git archive` into a clean scratch\\n  directory (independent of dev's own working copy) and ran\\n  `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` myself: `Ran 2 tests in 0.000s — OK`,\\n  exit code 0.\\n\\nAll three mission criteria (src/greet.py with the specified greet(name),\\ntests/test_greet.py covering a normal name and the empty string, and a clean\\n`unittest discover` run) are independently confirmed met.\\n\\n## Process notes\\n\\n- Single dispatch to dev (d002) sufficed; no rework was needed.\\n- dev's reply flagged `dirty: true` in its own working tree at reply time,\\n  but the committed branch itself was clean and matched the reply's claims,\\n  so this did not affect acceptance.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

